# 基本文章編集で開いた仮身を見えている所の外へスクロールする (design 11.3), for tools/ui_run.py:
# a text of twelve paragraphs, three paragraphs of two links each taller than closed (heightpx
# 31: opened, their object's text shown inside, as records TADjs wrote have them) and thirty
# paragraphs after (xml, xmlbig into a copy of 基本文章編集 made by mkbig), opened in the
# desktop's own text editor (docproc kernel) and then in the process (pdoc), and wound down by
# the wheel a notch at a time until the links have gone out at the top. What is inside a link
# must stay inside its box: a part of the window drawn again that misses the box (the strip
# a scroll brings in) must not get the link's contents. The shot after the wheel
# (vlink_*_scrolled) is compared with the same place drawn whole again by 表示 > 再表示
# (vlink_*_whole), inside the window where the text is (101,125 to 682,482 of the screen), and
# the desktop's with the process's.
# The menu opens with 閉じる on the pointer's row the first time (表示 60 below) and with the
# item chosen last afterwards (the process's after the desktop's); 表示's own opens with its
# first row on 表示's row, 再表示 100 below. Keys: Ctrl+E 08 01.
docproc kernel
mkbig doc 1
